cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "A harmonized fast-fashion garment-variant dataset for textile circularity and sustainability assessment"
message: "If you use this dataset or code, please cite the archived Zenodo release."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Li
    given-names: Kai
    affiliation: "Chair of Operations Management, RWTH Aachen University"
  - family-names: Walther
    given-names: Grit
    affiliation: "Chair of Operations Management, RWTH Aachen University"
date-released: 2026-05-03
version: "1.0.0"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20006389"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.20006389"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
abstract: "This dataset contains 47,522 colour-specific garment variants derived from publicly accessible H&M and Uniqlo product pages in the United Kingdom and Australia. The release includes a final component-normalized JSONL dataset, preprocessing scripts, CSV mapping tables, and TXT processing summaries for textile sorting and fibre-to-fibre recycling analysis."
keywords:
  - textile recycling
  - garment data
  - automated textile sorting
  - fibre-to-fibre recycling
  - circular economy
  - industrial ecology
  - fast fashion
  - material composition
  - component normalization
